00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.990
But not only do we need
to make it exposed,

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.370
we needed to make it easy.

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:20.940
Terabytes and terabytes
of data moving around.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.130
Automotive's a pretty
legacy industry.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:25.435
Boy, they love their flat files.

00:20:25.435 --> 00:20:26.310
But that didn't work.

00:20:26.310 --> 00:20:27.870
You can't move the
data fast enough--

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.130
at a high enough velocity--

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:33.060
without exposing some
sort of API interface.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:36.495
Our customers, they were
all internal and external--

00:20:36.495 --> 00:20:38.430
both data providers
and data consumers.

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.720
And so not only did our API
platform have to expose data,

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.328
but it also had to
ingest and ingress

00:20:44.328 --> 00:20:45.870
additional data from
other providers,

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:47.912
other teams within Urban
Science, and other teams

00:20:47.912 --> 00:20:48.803
externally.

00:20:48.803 --> 00:20:50.220
So we needed APIs
on the front end

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.345
to collect that data, and
then APIs on the back-end

00:20:52.345 --> 00:20:54.430
to also egress it back out.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:56.070
So why did we choose Apigee?

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.350
Back in '16-- that
was before they were

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.060
bought by Google, actually.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:02.150
We partnered with
Apigee and then

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.250
two weeks later, we learned
that Google acquired them.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:08.130
I heard that news, I'm
like, good decision.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:14.010
But we needed and we required
proper, mature API management--

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:18.130
not, I think I understand APIs.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.540
But really API management.

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.340
Somebody who
understood the needs

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:26.230
of the security, the needs of
the auditing and the analytics.

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:27.760
We needed something
that was easy--

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.820
easy to build, easy to maintain,
and easy for developers

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.590
to get access to.

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:34.155
We didn't want to
reinvent the wheel.

00:21:34.155 --> 00:21:36.280
We didn't want to build
all of that infrastructure.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:39.430
We wanted to focus on building
our microservices, our APIs,

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:41.267
and get them out to market.

00:21:41.267 --> 00:21:43.600
And again, we didn't want to
create that security layer.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.260
I know, I sound like
a broken record.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:47.680
But that security layer
is super, super important

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.420
with the sensitivity
of the data.

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.510
So the C4 Marketing
Intelligence Cloud--

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.210
that is our API product today.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.210
Fully integrated with Apigee.

