00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:32.128
So what are some of our
benefits and why it matters?

00:22:32.128 --> 00:22:34.420
"Bird Box," if you all see
it, is a great movie, right?

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:35.170
Fantastic.

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:37.240
But being blind is terrible.

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.370
It's absolutely terrible.

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:39.530
And without proper
API management,

00:22:39.530 --> 00:22:42.100
we were completely blind to
what was going on in the system.

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:44.530
We couldn't see what our
customers were seeing.

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:47.233
We couldn't see what our
developers were experiencing.

00:22:47.233 --> 00:22:48.400
So we were completely blind.

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:51.460
We needed that real-time
visibility into our production

00:22:51.460 --> 00:22:54.397
API behavior, so that we
could respond proactively,

00:22:54.397 --> 00:22:56.230
as opposed to waiting
for the telephone call

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:58.390
from an angry development
team saying, hey guys,

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:00.940
your stuff's broken.

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:03.820
Those calls are terrible
if you're an ops team.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:06.640
We needed API management
to allow our teams

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:08.560
to view that real-time
usage, so that we

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.860
could make critical, proactive
decisions about scale.

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:15.373
When you're at 1,000
transactions a day,

00:23:15.373 --> 00:23:17.290
that's a lot different
than 1,000 transactions

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.310
a second, right?

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:20.553
And the underlying
infrastructure

00:23:20.553 --> 00:23:21.720
that's required to run that?

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:22.825
It matters.

00:23:22.825 --> 00:23:24.700
So some of the challenges
that we experienced

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:26.710
before we put that
monitoring in place,

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.530
and before Apigee
introduced API monitoring?

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:30.880
Again, we were blind.

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:32.230
The clients would let us know.

00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:36.460
I think the worst day was when
I had three or four development

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:37.340
teams--

00:23:37.340 --> 00:23:39.970
two internal and one external--
send us emails telling us

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:41.860
